/backups

# user-uploaded Doc images — machine-local content, not source (see app/api/uploads/image)
/public/uploads

# DATABASES. This is not a tidiness entry — it is load-bearing.
#
# The Pterodactyl install script ends with `git clean -fd`, which deletes untracked files. Ignored
# files are spared (removing those needs -x), so these entries are the only thing standing between
# the live database and every Re-install. Without them, each Re-install silently wiped all
# production data — which is what kept leaving sessions orphaned ("Not authenticated" on every
# action while apparently logged in) and forced workspaces to be recreated over and over.
#
# NOTE THE PATH. Production's DATABASE_URL is `file:./siqt.db`, which reads like the repo root but
# is NOT: Prisma resolves a relative SQLite path against the SCHEMA FILE's directory, so the real
# database lives at `prisma/siqt.db`. A first attempt at this fix ignored `/siqt.db` and protected
# nothing at all — caught only by looking for the file on the server and finding it one directory
# down. Match on the whole directory rather than one filename so a renamed or newly-added database
# can't silently fall outside this again.
#
# Never run `git clean -fdx` against a production checkout: `-x` removes ignored files too, which
# defeats all of this.
/prisma/*.db
/prisma/*.db-journal
/prisma/*.db-wal
/prisma/*.db-shm
